-- title:
--   Inertia at a Taylor–Wiles prime acts by diamond operators
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field, $p$ a prime with $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and $\bar\rho$ a two-dimensional residual Galois representation over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$ (a rank-two module with a Galois action trivial on some finite extension of $\mathbb Q$) which is absolutely irreducible. Let $S$ be a finite set of naturals containing all prime divisors of $N \neq 0$, let $r$ be a prime not dividing $N$, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$N$ Hecke algebra with $S$ omitted (the $\mathbb Z$-algebra generated by the $T_\ell$, $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, and $U_q$, $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$, acting on cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$) to $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$ such that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ outside $S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell \in P$ non-invertible and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Let $qv : \mathrm{Fin}\,t \to \mathbb N$ be injective with each $qv\,i$ prime, outside $S$ and distinct from $r$, let $\pi\Delta_i : (\mathbb Z/qv\,i)^\times \to \mathbb Z/p^{v_p(qv\,i - 1)}$ be homomorphisms, and $\alpha : \mathrm{Fin}\,t \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$. With $L = N(\prod_i qv\,i)r$, $H_r = \ker((\mathbb Z/L)^\times \to (\mathbb Z/r)^\times)$ and $H_Q = H_r \cap \ker(\pi\Delta)$, assume the operators attached to the generators commute pairwise and commute with all diamond operators; let $T$ be the resulting Hecke ring, the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of endomorphisms of the localised cohomology module generated by the Hecke and diamond operators. Assume $T$ is local, Noetherian and complete for its maximal-adic topology, that $\mathcal O \to T$ is a local homomorphism with $T$ finite over $\mathcal O$ and with $\mathcal O$ surjecting onto the residue field of $T$. Let $\rho'$ be a Galois representation on a free $T$-module of rank two, adically continuous, whose trace at each Frobenius at a prime $\ell$ outside $S$ not dividing $L$ is the Hecke operator $T_\ell$ of $T$, and whose residual representation is isomorphic to the base change of $\bar\rho$ along the induced map of residue fields. Fix $i$ with $p \mid qv\,i - 1$, assume $\alpha_i$ is a root of $X^2 - \theta(T_{qv\,i})X + qv\,i$ with $2\alpha_i \neq \theta(T_{qv\,i})$, and let $\mathrm{cyc}$ be a homomorphism from the Galois group to $(\mathbb Z/qv\,i)^\times$ with $\sigma\mu = \mu^{\mathrm{cyc}(\sigma)}$ for all $qv\,i$-th roots of unity $\mu$. Then for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $qv\,i$ is not a unit there is a $T$-basis $b_0, b_1$ of the representation space of $\rho'$ such that every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup attached to $P$ fixes $b_1$, and acts on $b_0$ by the diamond operator $\langle u\rangle$ for every $u \in H_r$ whose $i$-th component matches $\pi\Delta_i(\mathrm{cyc}(\sigma))$ and whose other components are trivial.
--
--   This is the local–global compatibility at a Taylor–Wiles prime $q_i$: on a suitable basis, inertia at $q_i$ acts on the modular deformation diagonally, trivially on one line and through the diamond operators of the $p$-part of $(\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times$ on the other. It is the ingredient that makes the Hecke module over the augmented level an $\mathcal O[\Delta_Q]$-module compatibly with the Galois action, and it is used in the constructions of the adic Galois representation carried by the Hecke ring acting on the localised cohomology module.
